  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to HIV and AIDS, Poverty and Gender Inequalities in KwaZulu Natal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcomes
1. A reduction in the prevalence/ new infection of the pandemic/ HIV in the province.
2. Decreased levels of poverty combined with an increase in sustainable livelihoods. 
3. Improved gender justice at household, community and provincial level. 
4. Established functional Coordination Network for the province responding to the gender, HIV&amp;AIDS, economic and social injustices.

The KwaZulu Natal Council of Churches (KZNCC) and partners intend to implement an ambitious programme titled &#x2018;&#x2018;Responding to HIV and AIDS, Poverty and Gender Inequalities in KwaZulu Natal&#x2019;&#x2019; throughout the province in response to the unique challenges faced. This programme is built on the backbone of 10 years experience and lessons learnt in the province. KZNCC has become the hub for civil society responses in the province bringing together diverse groups such as churches, traditional leadership and other religions. This will be achieved through mobilising communities, churches, communities to campaign and advocate for their rights. More importantly, the programme will work at community level to change perceptions, views and cultural practices that are detrimental and catalyst of violence, HIV and AIDS and crime. To date, KZNCC has recorded notable success in bringing changes within the Church, as Church leaders have become active agents of change in addressing the challenges and problems faced by residents of KZN.</narrative>
  </description>
